Immersive, Impressive, Addictive...the more you play it, the more you love it...
I'm just six years late to start playing Dead Space. I must confess it wasn't my favorite game sytle until last week. So I decided to go through it and here I am: looking foward to go playing through the dead space trilogy...amazing game, awesome details, interesting atmosphere, very good sound effects and cinematics.
The surprising features:
1. The game engine is smooth with loading screens only in chapter transitions;
2. The level design is amasingly perfect and creepy as well;
3. Overall plot is very good and its main and secondary objectives are interesting;
4. There are two mini games on it;
5. Weapons visual, sound, and physical effects are really cool. No standard military weapons;
6. Enemies are creepy and disgusting...but funny to kill;
7. Boss fights are good;
8. There are 'store feature' that allow you buying and selling in game items;
9. Weapon upgrades are enjoyable and worth;
10. In game player interfaces are well developed and animated (cargo lift buttoms, weapon benches, stores, control pannels);
11. Looting system provides well balanced sort of items throughout the whole game (ammo, medkits, money, etc);
12. Zero gravity missions and fights are as awesome as tense;
13. Different sort of weapons provides an interesting replayability. Try only few weapons at a time and see the difference in game play and difficulty level;
14. Story telling is well balanced between direct dialogs and in game information (video logs, text logs, cut scenes, etc).
Overall, the game is still worth playing even at 6 years later. Just play it and have fun.

Not exactly what I was expecting, but very good nonetheless. I was expecting a bigger world, tons of sidequests and all that makes a epic RPG game.
Pros:
- The world is beautifully drawn;
- The combat system is great;
- Workshop (I'll eventually come back because of it;
- The dialogs is very well detailed and well written;
- The music is very good;
Cons:
- There's not much to do besides the main quest;
- Checkpoint saves;
- Bad interface cleary designed for mobile devices;
- Basically no loot;
- No trade between characters;
Besides the cons, I enjoyed big time this game and will be back for the workshop. Recommended.
